cat > "$DIR/README.md" <<MD
# $TITLE

A [Synapse](https://synapse.kakde.eu) book. **This repository is the book**: the chapters sit at
the root, and \`book.json\` carries the identity.

## The contract

- \`book.json\` holds \`title\`, \`description\`, \`tags\` and the \`slug\` that fixes the URL.
  Treat the slug as immutable once published — every link and media path embeds it.
- **Chapters are directories, lessons are \`.md\` files.** Ordering comes from the \`NN-\` prefix,
  which is stripped from the URL. \`index.md\` sorts first; unnumbered sorts last.
- **Every lesson needs frontmatter** with \`title\` and \`summary\`.
- **A problem** is a directory of three co-named files: \`<stem>.md\` with \`kind: problem\`,
  \`<stem>.tests.json\` (cases marked \`"sample": true\` are the only ones the browser sees), and
  \`<stem>.editorial.md\`.
- **Media** lives at \`_media/$SLUG/<lesson-slug>/…\`, referenced as
  \`![alt](/media/$SLUG/<lesson-slug>/file.svg)\`.
- Names starting with \`_\` or \`.\`, and the \`examples/\` and \`c4/\` directories, never render.
  Neither does this README.

Where the book sits in the library is set when the repository is registered, not here.

## Before you push

\`\`\`sh
dev-tools/validate-book .   # from a synapse checkout, pointed at this directory
\`\`\`

It runs the server's own walker, so what it reports is what the site will do.
MD

mkdir -p "$DIR/.github/workflows"
cat > "$DIR/.github/workflows/validate.yml" <<'YAML'
name: validate

# The book has to render before it is merged. This runs the SERVER'S walker, so the gate and the
# site agree by construction rather than by review.
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:

jobs:
  validate:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          path: book
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          repository: ani2fun/synapse
          path: synapse
      - uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable
      - uses: Swatinem/rust-cache@v2
        with:
          workspaces: synapse
      - name: validate-book
        working-directory: synapse
        run: ./dev-tools/validate-book ../book

  # The /c4 viewer is ONE merged workspace built in the spine repository, so a diagram changed
  # HERE still has to rebuild it there. Skipped when the token is absent — the spine also rebuilds
  # nightly, which bounds the staleness to a day rather than forever.
  rebuild-diagrams:
    needs: validate
    if: github.event_name == 'push'
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - id: changed
        run: |
          if git diff --name-only "${{ github.event.before }}" "${{ github.sha }}" | grep -q '\.c4$'; then
            echo "c4=true" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
          fi
      - name: dispatch the merged workspace rebuild
        if: steps.changed.outputs.c4 == 'true' && env.TOKEN != ''
        env:
          TOKEN: ${{ secrets.SPINE_DISPATCH_TOKEN }}
        run: |
          curl -fsS -X POST \
            -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
            -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
            https://api.github.com/repos/ani2fun/synapse-content/dispatches \
            -d '{"event_type":"c4-changed"}'
YAML

echo "✓ scaffolded $TITLE at $DIR"
echo "  next: dev-tools/validate-book $DIR"
